    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d851">

                <pb facs="1132" n="1122" xml:id="pg1122"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/8–1445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-14T14:00:00+07:00">August 14, 1945—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 15—7:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1354. Re your 1205, August 6, Embassy considers advantageous your proposal for
                    use of gold bullion to combat effect of inflation on Chinese war production.
                    Taking up questions informally with responsible Chinese officials would be an
                    excellent way of ascertaining whether Chinese intend to use gold to combat
                    inflation. In view of present obscure situation, however, suggest we delay
                    discussing matter informally with Chinese. Please repeat to Treasury.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
